Since, $|z|+z=3+i$

Let $z=a+i b,$ then



|z|+z=3+i \Rightarrow \sqrt{a^{2}+b^{2}}+a+i b=3+i



Compare real and imaginary coefficients on both sides



\begin{array}{l}

b=1, \sqrt{a^{2}+b^{2}}+a=3 \\

\sqrt{a^{2}+1}=3-a \\

a^{2}+1=a^{2}+9-6 a \\

6 a=8 \Rightarrow a=\frac{4}{3}

\end{array}



Then,



|z|=\sqrt{\left(\frac{4}{3}\right)^{2}+1}=\sqrt{\frac{16}{9}+1}=\frac{5}{3}
